WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:05.959
It's really important for me not to be hyperbolic
in this segment because this is so serious,

00:00:05.959 --> 00:00:06.959
but to act

00:00:06.959 --> 00:00:12.790
Lee communicate to you the dire situation
that we're in with regard to the 2020 election.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:17.930
The language might sound like what is normally
hyperbolic language, but in this case it just

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.200
accurately reflects the circumstances.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.960
What I'm talking about is that the 2020 election
is not going to be a fair election in what

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:30.050
we, most of us imagine when we say a fair
election, if a Democrat is to defeat Donald

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:35.300
Trump in 2020 it's going to be despite all
sorts of underhanded tactics and endless betrayals

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.789
of the type of election that our founding
fathers wanted us to have year in and year

00:00:39.789 --> 00:00:40.789
out.

00:00:40.789 --> 00:00:46.729
Foreign interference happened in 2016 Trump
just said to George Stephanopoulos on national

00:00:46.729 --> 00:00:55.219
TV that he'd welcome help again in 2020 republicans
including Mitch Mcconnell or simply blocking

00:00:55.219 --> 00:01:00.429
any bill to secure the election from foreign
interference, which we've talked about.

00:01:00.429 --> 00:01:05.280
The big voting machine lobbyists are now donating
to Mitch Mcconnell's campaign, which we've

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.690
talked about voter suppression, not voter
fraud.

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:14.189
Remember voter suppression, which is this
package of policies that Republicans have

00:01:14.189 --> 00:01:21.549
been pushing for decades to limit voting hours,
to limit voting locations in poorer nonwhite,

00:01:21.549 --> 00:01:28.140
democratic leaning areas, combined with using
the boogeyman of voter fraud as a sort of

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:36.590
straw man to justify voter purges and voter
id laws and so much more gerrymandering, which

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:42.120
already favors Republicans because of the
urban rural divide just systemically, but

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:47.360
it's used even more grossly to favor Republicans
and how the congressional districts are currently

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:52.840
drawn the very real possibility that Donald
Trump, if at any point he truly starts to

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:58.820
believe that he is losing rather than writing
off all the polls, it's fake panics and tries

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:01.130
to get us into a military conflict.

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:06.569
It could be Iran, could be Venezuela, could
be, I mean almost anything with this guy that

00:02:06.569 --> 00:02:11.940
does affect voters and it will be another
thing that Democrats and whoever is the eventual

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.950
democratic nominee is going to need to overcome.

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:21.270
So what I want to convey to you today is that
even if we deal with any three of these four

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:27.030
major ways in which this is not going to be
a fair election, it is going to be an uphill

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:32.000
battle where the Democratic nominee, whoever
he or she ultimately is, is going to need

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:40.240
to overcome significant slanting in the infrastructure
of this election in order to actually win.

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:45.520
Now, that doesn't mean that it's impossible,
but what you need to do is immediately put

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:49.630
out of your mind the idea that it might be
a fair election because it's just not going

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:50.830
to be okay.

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:55.290
There's a rolling stone article pointing out
that Republicans are more than willing to

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:58.180
help make this an unfair election.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:04.380
So if you are even considering like for a
split second not voting because of all of

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.930
these things, you should rethink that.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:07.930
Okay?

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:14.000
If you say the election is fundamentally slanted
towards Donald Trump's reelection, so I'm

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:18.480
not going to vote, that is the exact wrong
reaction to be having.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:25.150
You need to vote because your vote is so much
more important given that this is going to

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:31.630
require if the Democratic candidate is going
to win, uh, going above and beyond all of

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:36.370
these systemic factors that have the playing
field slanted in the direction of Donald Trump

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:37.660
the last midterm.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:38.660
Okay?

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:42.900
The 2018 midterms, that also was not a fair
election.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:47.830
Democrats were able to pick up records, seats
in the house because people voted in such

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:54.150
numbers that we were stronger than the lack
of fairness that is implicit in the system

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:57.700
in a way that tilts towards Republicans in
the ways that I described.

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:03.470
So you need to realize that we're fighting
people who don't care about fairness, okay?

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:08.410
The Republican Party decided decades ago that
they don't care about being fair or behaving

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:13.380
appropriately or running elections in a way
that is in line with what the founding fathers

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:14.380
wanted.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:15.740
This is basically sport to them.

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:16.740
Okay?

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:17.740
It's just wins and losses.

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:18.740
That's all it is.

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:20.260
It's strikes and balls or whatever.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:22.900
All that matters is wins on the board.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:30.390
If the policy's destroy farmers in the Midwest,
if they destroy democracy at its core, whatever,

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:36.010
if they destroy the middleclass, as long as
this Republican Party sees that they are quote,

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:41.820
winning and checking off the right boxes on
the scoreboard, that is all that they care

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:42.820
about.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:47.750
So on the one hand, we can't stoop to their
level because we are not like them.

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:53.510
But if we don't start winning somehow, we
will never take them out of power.

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:55.090
And that's what the left needs to understand.

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:59.370
And that's why a lot of my focus lately has
been on trying to unite the left rather than

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:05.080
allowing these arbitrary and rigid divisions
of the left to fracture the left.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:10.510
Because we're up against significant unfairness
in this upcoming election.

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:14.580
So if you don't vote, we don't even have a
chance.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:19.580
Even if you do, we still need to overcome
all the injustice of the system that they've

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:26.720
successfully put in place over the last several
decades for their own gain at their own, for

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.260
their own advantage.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:34.620
So that should I hope, motivate you to vote
rather than say that I'm not even going to,

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:37.101
if you disagree with my take on this, I want
to hear from you.

00:05:37.101 --> 00:05:43.090
If you think that this scenario means you
shouldn't even bother voting, I vehemently

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:47.060
disagree with you and I hope you'll call in
later this week when I take live calls and

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:51.120
confront me about it because it's something
I absolutely want to talk to you about because

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:52.810
it is so important.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:53.810
It is.

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:58.241
I, I, I don't want to be hyperbolic, but the
reality is extreme and we need to understand

00:05:58.241 --> 00:05:58.242
that.

